  "created": "2026-08-30T17:24:59.597Z",
  "description": "Authors \".cbv\" video files in both of their flavours - the WebM-profile one that FFmpeg writes in a single pass, and the bespoke one that FFmpeg's IVF and Ogg output is muxed into by CodeBrix.VideoPlayback's own muxer - from one request object: AV1 video, Opus or Vorbis audio, WebVTT or SubRip caption tracks with their language, name and flags, chapters from an FFmpeg metadata file, an optional colour-grade chain baked to one lookup table, device-class presets, a dry run that renders every command line without starting anything, and a streamable-profile report over the finished file. This is a DEVELOPER-MACHINE tool: it drives the FFmpeg on the authoring workstation through CodeBrix.VideoProcessing and never belongs in a shipped application.",
